  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Twenty-Four. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '24 is a mathematical card game: use four numbers (from four cards) and only +, Ã¢Ë†â€™, Ãƒâ€”, ÃƒÂ· (and parentheses) to make exactly 24. All four numbers must be used once. First to call a correct solution wins the four cards (or they go to opponent); play until one player has no cards. Popular in China since at least the 1960s (Shanghai); also played in North America.',
    objective: "Be the first player to complete a valid logic pyramid whose final output matches the required binary output on that player's side.",
    gameplay: 'Lay initial binary cards as the shared base, then take turns drawing and playing logic gate cards into a narrowing pyramid. Every placed gate must correctly transform its two input cards into the output shown on that gate. Continue until one player completes a coherent pyramid to the top output.',
    keyRules: [
      'Cards represent binary values and Boolean logic gates.',
      'Each gate card must be logically valid for the two cards feeding it.',
      'The game uses draw-one-play-one tempo, so blocking the opponent while preserving valid gate sequences is central.',
